discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Components are in the order Tarjan’s algorithm completes them, on a depth-first search","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with roots in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order and successors in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"text":" order (the order of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"NetworkX, petgraph and Boost). That is a reverse topological order of the condensation:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every edge between components goes from a later component to an earlier one, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed()"},{"text":" lists the components with every edge going forward. Each component lists its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so on a graph whose vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions are insertion order (","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), one sort puts the components in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"insertion order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.stronglyConnectedComponents().sorted { graph.vertices.firstIndex(of: $0.first!)! < graph.vertices.firstIndex(of: $1.first!)! }"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/stronglyconnectedcomponents()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/stronglyConnectedC